# CometWeb Agent Skills routing

Load skills from `~/.cursor/skills/` (symlinked from `platforms/agent-skills`). Prefer
**one primary skill** per turn unless the user wants a multi-step workflow — then use
`skill-orchestrator` (single thread) or `skill-orchestrator-multiagent` (one subagent
per step). Hand off via CW-AIP envelopes when outputs feed another skill.

## Primary routing

| Intent | Skill |
| --- | --- |
| Multi-skill workflow, single thread | `skill-orchestrator` |
| Multi-skill workflow, one subagent per skill / Task per step | `skill-orchestrator-multiagent` |
| Whole repo/project → baseline roadmap to target state | `repo-to-roadmap` |
| Weekly control loop on existing roadmap/state | `product-operator` |
| Pinned RC/build + environment → GO/NO_GO/DEFER | `release-readiness` |
| Evidence Pack / claim verification (no decision) | `evidence-researcher` |
| Explicit Council / high-stakes multi-domain decision | `ai-council` |
| Competitor monitoring, deltas, watchlist | `competitive-intelligence` |
| External product pattern → adaptation | `product-teardown` |
| Design partner program / cohort | `design-partner-finder` |
| Support → incident → engineering loop | `customer-ops` |
| Live web QA / click-through / a11y | `web-app-auditor` |
| SEO/GEO/AEO visibility audit | `seo-geo-aeo-maxxing` |
| Humanize / de-AI-tell prose (PL/EN) | `ai-humanize` |

## Collision guardrails

- **Repo to Roadmap** — first-time or delta whole-project baseline; not weekly sprint ops.
- **Product Operator** — reconciled next actions; not from-scratch roadmap.
- **Release Readiness** — requires identifiable release candidate + environment; score never overrides gates.
- **AI Council** — explicit invocation only; not routine research or triage.
- **Evidence Researcher** — upstream of decisions; never issues GO/NO_GO alone.
- **Skill Orchestrator** — sequences specialists in one thread; does not replace domain skills.
- **Skill Orchestrator Multiagent** — launches subagents; parent must not run domain steps inline.

## Execution

1. Read the skill's `SKILL.md` before acting.
2. Run deterministic scripts in `skills/<name>/scripts/` when available.
3. Polish for product/CRM/ops replies when the user writes in Polish.
4. Inter-skill handoffs: `platforms/agent-skills/protocol/cw-interchange-v1.md`.
